[Intro — spoken, over Rhodes]
Mmm…
Sun going down across the canyon,
Still a little light in here.
Pull up a chair, baby.
[Verse 1]
Golden evening on the window,
Coffee cooling by my side.
Had a beautiful machine,
Never felt like it was mine.
Then I gave the night a new shade,
Let the windows fall in line.
Found myself still making changes
With the sunrise in my eyes.
[Pre-Chorus]
A little room to move,
A little space to grow.
My hands have found a rhythm
They forgot they used to know.
[Chorus]
Oh, Oh-Ma-Chee,
Let me make myself at home.
Got a little blue, a little amber,
Got a feeling of my own.
Oh, Oh-Ma-Chee,
Hear those keys beneath my hands.
I came here just to change one thing,
Now I’m making other plans.
(Making other plans…)
[Verse 2]
Someone asks about the colors,
Why I take the time I do.
Come sit down beside me,
See what happens with that blue.
Now the hours come a little easier,
Got some music, got some flow.
And the thing I made this evening,
You can take and make your own.
[Pre-Chorus]
Leave a little door unlocked,
Let somebody wander through.
They might find a way to take it
Somewhere beautiful and new.
[Chorus]
Oh, Oh-Ma-Chee,
Let me make myself at home.
Got a little blue, a little amber,
Got a feeling of my own.
Oh, Oh-Ma-Chee,
Hear those keys beneath my hands.
I came here just to change one thing,
Now I’m making other plans.
(Making other plans…)
[Bridge — half-time, strings rise]
Outpost calling through the static,
Haven underneath two moons.
I’ve been dreaming up a world here
In this quiet little room.
There’s a light beyond the mountains,
There’s a coast I haven’t seen.
Let the bass line take me over,
Put that ocean on my screen.
[Break — backing vocals, guitar fills]
(Make yourself at home…)
Move a little closer.
(Make yourself at home…)
Stay a little longer.
Ain’t it good to find
Something you can call your own?
[Final Chorus — full band]
Oh, Oh-Ma-Chee,
Let me make myself at home.
Got a little blue, a little amber,
Got a feeling of my own.
Oh, Oh-Ma-Chee,
There’s still so much left to do.
I’ll leave a little light here,
And a place beside me, too.
And a place beside me, too.
(A place beside me, too…)
[Outro — fading vamp]
One more color,
One more tune.
Morning sunlight
In my room.
(Make yourself at home…)
Mmm, I believe I will.
